var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"#RadarData","page":"Home","text":"RadarData provides data structures and utilities for working with synthetic aperture radar (SAR) data. The package handles radar phase history data, SAR imagery, position/navigation/timing (PNT) information, and coordinate transformations.","title":"RadarData"},{"category":"section","location":"#Overview","page":"Home","text":"The main components of RadarData.jl are:\n\nVPH (Video Phase History): Core data structure for radar returns\nSARImage: Container for SAR image data with georeferencing\nPNT (Position, Navigation, Timing): Platform state information\nCoordinate Systems: Transformations between ECEF, ENU, LLA, and horizon coordinates\nRange Compression: Pulse compression utilities\nImage Metadata: Structures for SAR image formation (PFA knots, image planes)\nFFT Utilities: Convenience functions for FFT operations","title":"Overview"},{"category":"section","location":"#Constants","page":"Home","text":"","title":"Constants"},{"category":"section","location":"#Video-Phase-History-(VPH)","page":"Home","text":"The core data type maintained by RadarData.jl is the video phase history, or VPH.  This structure contains range-compressed radar returns along with associated metadata including platform positions, timing, and frequency information.","title":"Video Phase History (VPH)"},{"category":"section","location":"#VPH-Type","page":"Home","text":"","title":"VPH Type"},{"category":"section","location":"#VPH-Metadata-Functions","page":"Home","text":"These functions extract or compute metadata from VPH objects:","title":"VPH Metadata Functions"},{"category":"section","location":"#VPH-Domain-Conversion","page":"Home","text":"Convert between frequency domain and range (fast-time) domain:","title":"VPH Domain Conversion"},{"category":"section","location":"#VPH-Data-Selection","page":"Home","text":"Extract subsets and pad VPH data:","title":"VPH Data Selection"},{"category":"section","location":"#SAR-Image","page":"Home","text":"SAR images with georeferencing and metadata.","title":"SAR Image"},{"category":"section","location":"#SARImage-Type","page":"Home","text":"","title":"SARImage Type"},{"category":"section","location":"#SARImage-Functions","page":"Home","text":"","title":"SARImage Functions"},{"category":"section","location":"#Position,-Navigation,-and-Timing-(PNT)","page":"Home","text":"PNT structures store platform state information including position, velocity, and attitude.","title":"Position, Navigation, and Timing (PNT)"},{"category":"section","location":"#PNT-Types","page":"Home","text":"","title":"PNT Types"},{"category":"section","location":"#PNT-Functions","page":"Home","text":"","title":"PNT Functions"},{"category":"section","location":"#Coordinate-Transformations","page":"Home","text":"Functions for working with coordinate systems.  VPH objects are always expressed in a local coordinate system, assumed to  be the East-North-Up (ENU) tangent plane to the WGS84 ellipsoid at vph.lla.","title":"Coordinate Transformations"},{"category":"section","location":"#Range-Compression","page":"Home","text":"Pulse compression utilities:","title":"Range Compression"},{"category":"section","location":"#Image-Metadata","page":"Home","text":"Structures for SAR image formation and metadata.","title":"Image Metadata"},{"category":"section","location":"#Image-Plane","page":"Home","text":"","title":"Image Plane"},{"category":"section","location":"#PFA-Knots","page":"Home","text":"Polar Format Algorithm metadata structure:","title":"PFA Knots"},{"category":"section","location":"#FFT-Utilities","page":"Home","text":"Convenience functions for FFT operations:","title":"FFT Utilities"},{"category":"section","location":"#Support-for-Conventions","page":"Home","text":"Common conventions are encapsulated in function handles for easy recall:","title":"Support for Conventions"},{"category":"section","location":"#Index","page":"Home","text":"","title":"Index"},{"category":"constant","location":"#RadarData.c0","page":"Home","text":"c0 = 299792458\n\nSpeed of light in a vaccuum, expressed in meters per second\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.c0"},{"category":"type","location":"#RadarData.VPH","page":"Home","text":"Video Phase History data structure.\n\nEach column represents a single pulse of returned data, which has been range-compressed. The columns may represent either frequency or fast-time data, according to the value of range_domain. Data may be either ComplexF32 or ComplexF64, but position and timing metadata will be retained at Float64 precision.\n\ndata::Array{Complex{T}, 2} where T<:AbstractFloat: Complex-valued data matrix, frequency (or fast-time / range) by slow-time\nfreq_list_hz::Vector{Float64}: Frequency list, in Hz\nref_range_m::Vector{Float64}: Two-way range to the center range bin for each pulse\nslow_time_s::Vector{Float64}: Per-pulse collection time, in seconds relative to ref_time_s\nref_time_s::Float64: Reference time, in posix time (seconds since Unix Epoch)\ntx_pos_enu::Matrix{Float64}: Position of transmitter in East-North-Up (ENU), meters\nrx_pos_enu::Matrix{Float64}: Position of receiver (ENU, meters)\nsrp_enu::Matrix{Float64}: Position of (possibly shifting) scene reference point (ENU, meters)\nsrp_lla::StaticArraysCore.SVector{3, Float64}: Fixed scene reference position for ENU frame in latitude (deg), longitude (deg), altitude (m)\nkernel_sign::Float64: FFT sign convention for transformation from frequency to fast-time domain, default is -1\nc_eff_ms::Float64: Effective speed of light (m/s)\nrange_domain::Bool: Whether the first dimension represents frequency or range (fast-time)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.VPH"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.VPH-Tuple{AbstractArray{Complex{T}, 2} where T<:AbstractFloat, AbstractVector, AbstractVector, AbstractVector, AbstractMatrix}","page":"Home","text":"VPH(data, freq_list_hz, ref_range_m, slow_time_s, tx_pos_enu; kw_args)\n\nConvenience constructor for VPH type.\n\nKeyword Arguments:\n\nref_time_s = 0\nrx_pos_enu = tx_pos_enu\nsrp_enu = zeros(3,1)\nsrp_lla = [39.729866; -84.077144; 0]\nkernel_sign = -1\nc_eff_ms = c0\nrange_domain = false\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.VPH"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.VPH-Tuple{Int64, Int64}","page":"Home","text":"VPH(n_freqs, n_pulses)\n\nConvenience constructor for generating a quick test VPH of a given size.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.VPH"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.pri-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"Approximate pulse repetition interval of VPH.\nAssumes constant pulse spacing.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.pri"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.get_freq_list","page":"Home","text":"get_freq_list(center_freq, bandwidth, num_freqs)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.get_freq_list"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.spatial_freqs-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"spatial_freqs(vph)\n\nFor frequency freqs in Hz, return the spatial frequency 2πf/c.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.spatial_freqs"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.bandwidth-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"bandwidth(vph)\n\nReturn the bandwidth spanned by VPH.freq_list_hz.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.bandwidth"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.center_freq-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"center_freq(vph)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.center_freq"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.range_res-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"range_res(vph)\n\nCompute two-way range resolution in meters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.range_res"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.velocity_res-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"velocity_res(vph)\n\nCompute two-way velocity resolution in meters per pulse.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.velocity_res"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.range_axis-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"range_axis(vph)\n\nCompute range axis (two-way meters) of range-Doppler image formed from VPH.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.range_axis"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.fast_time_axis-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"fast_time_axis(vph)\n\nCompute the range axis of the VPH, scaled to relative times of arrival, in seconds.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.fast_time_axis"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.velocity_axis-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"velocity_axis(vph)\n\nCompute velocity axis (m/pulse) of range-Doppler image formed from VPH.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.velocity_axis"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.time_axis-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"time_axis(vph)\n\nForm an equispaced list of times, spanning duration of VPH collection.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.time_axis"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.doppler_axis-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"doppler_axis(vph)\n\nCompute Doppler frequency axis (Hz) for range-Doppler map.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.doppler_axis"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.cross_range_extent-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"cross_range_extent(vph)\n\nCompute unambiguous cross range extent (in meters) around scene reference point.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.cross_range_extent"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.bistatic_angles-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"bistatic_angles(vph)\n\nCompute bistatic angle per-pulse.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.bistatic_angles"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.bisectors-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"bisectors(vph)\n\nReturn bistatic bisectors for VPH object.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.bisectors"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.range_dir_enu-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"range_dir_enu(vph)\n\nReturn a unit vector pointing towards the down-range direction, in ENU coordinates.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.range_dir_enu"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.cross_range_dir_enu-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"cross_range_dir_enu(vph)\n\nReturn a unit vector pointing towards the cross-range direction (positive velocity), in ENU coordinates.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.cross_range_dir_enu"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.bp_layover_projection-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"bp_layover_projection(vph)\n\nCompute approximate layover projection for ENU coordinates in short aperture backprojection imagery. Only appropriate for approximately monostatic collections.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.bp_layover_projection"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.azimuth_rad-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"Compute azimuth look direction, in radians.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.azimuth_rad"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.elevation_rad-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"Compute elevation look direction, in radians.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.elevation_rad"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.horizon_coords-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"Compute horizon coordinates (range, azimuth, elevation), in meters and radians.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.horizon_coords"},{"category":"function","location":"#Base.show","page":"Home","text":"show(io, vph)\n\nCustom display method for VPH.\n\n\n\n\n\nshow(io, image)\n\nCustom display method for SARImage.\n\n\n\n\n\nBase.show(io::IO, pfa_knots::PFAKnots)\n\nPretty-print PFAKnots structure with formatted field display.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.show"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.vph_to_rs!-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"vph_to_rs!(vph)\n\nConvert vph to range and slow-time data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.vph_to_rs!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.vph_to_rs-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"vph_to_rs(vph)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.vph_to_rs"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.rs_to_vph!-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"rs_to_vph!(vph)\n\nConvert range and slow-time data back to frequency and slow-time data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.rs_to_vph!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.rs_to_vph-Tuple{VPH}","page":"Home","text":"rs_to_vph(vph)\n\nConvert range and slow-time data back to frequency and slow-time data.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.rs_to_vph"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.freq_truncate!-Tuple{VPH, UnitRange{Int64}}","page":"Home","text":"freq_truncate!(vph,keep_idxs)\n\nTruncate frequency support of VPH to range of indices.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.freq_truncate!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.freq_truncate!-Tuple{VPH, Real, Real}","page":"Home","text":"freq_truncate!(vph, start_freq_hz, stop_freq_hz)\n\nTruncate frequency support of VPH to the range of frequencies specified by start_freq_hz and stop_freq_hz.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.freq_truncate!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.time_truncate!-Tuple{VPH, AbstractVector{Int64}}","page":"Home","text":"time_truncate!(vph, keep_idxs)\n\nTruncate time support of VPH to range of pulses.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.time_truncate!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.time_truncate!-Tuple{VPH, Real, Real}","page":"Home","text":"time_truncate!(vph, start_time_s, stop_time_s)\n\nTruncate VPH in time, as indicated by start and stop times.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.time_truncate!"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.extract_cpi-Tuple{VPH, AbstractVector{Int64}}","page":"Home","text":"extract_cpi(vph, cpi_idxs)\n\nExtract a sub-VPH from the given pulse indices. This is sometimes referred to as a Coherent Processing Interval (CPI).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.extract_cpi"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.freq_pad!","page":"Home","text":"freq_pad!(vph, num_top, num_bottom = num_top)\n\nZero-pad VPH in frequency domain, adding num_top frequency bins at the low end and num_bottom frequency bins at the high end.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.freq_pad!"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.range_pad!","page":"Home","text":"range_pad!(vph, num_top, num_bottom = num_top)\n\nZero-pad VPH in range (fast-time) domain, adding num_top range bins at the top and num_bottom range bins at the bottom.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.range_pad!"},{"category":"type","location":"#RadarData.SARImage","page":"Home","text":"SARImage\n\nStructure for containing SAR image data with axes and labels.\n\ndata::Array{Complex{T}, 2} where T<:AbstractFloat: Image pixel data. Expected to be either ComplexF32 or ComplexF64\nrow_axis::Vector{Float64}: Location of pixel grid centers, increasing down first dimension (row)\ncol_axis::Vector{Float64}: Location of pixel grid centers, increasing across second dimension (column)\nrow_label::String: Label for row axis\ncol_label::String: Label for column axis\nsrp_lla::StaticArraysCore.SVector{3, Float64}: Scene reference point in LLA coordinates\nsrp_pixel::StaticArraysCore.SVector{2, Int64}: Pixel corresponding to scene reference point\nrow_unit_vector::StaticArraysCore.SVector{3, Float64}: Unit vector pointing in direction of increasing first direction in ECEF coordinate frame\ncol_unit_vector::StaticArraysCore.SVector{3, Float64}: Unit vector pointing in direction of increasing second direction in ECEF coordinate frame\nalgorithm::String: Identifier for algorithm used to form the image\nfull_size::StaticArraysCore.SVector{2, Int64}: Full image size, if this image is a sub-image\nstart_idxs::StaticArraysCore.SVector{2, Int64}: Row and column index of the first pixel in the sub-image, relative to the full image\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.SARImage"},{"category":"method","location":"#RadarData.resolution-Tuple{SARImage}","page":"Home","text":"resolution(image)\n\nReturn static vector with pixel spacing in meters of SARImage in row and column axes.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.resolution"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.image_corners_ecef","page":"Home","text":"image_corners_ecef(image)\n\nReturn corners of image in ECEF coordinates. Order of columns is first row, first column; first row, last column; last row, last column; last row, first column. Note, this does not account for Earth curvature.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.image_corners_ecef"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.image_corners_lla","page":"Home","text":"image_corners_lla(image)\n\nReturn corners of image in LLA coordinates. Order of columns is first row, first column; first row, last column; last row, last column; last row, first column. Note, this does not account for Earth curvature.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.image_corners_lla"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.enu_frame","page":"Home","text":"enu_frame(image)\n\nReturn East-North-Up (ENU) coordinate frame centered on image SRP, expressed in relative ECEF coordinates.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.enu_frame"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.image_axes","page":"Home","text":"image_axes(image)\n\nReturn image axes, expressed in relative ECEF coordinates. Column order is down range, increasing cross range, and up out of imaging plane.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.image_axes"},{"category":"type","location":"#RadarData.PVAHeader","page":"Home","text":"Position, Velocity, Attitude message header. Corresponds to ASPN convention in aspn_schema/header.schema.json\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.PVAHeader"},{"category":"type","location":"#RadarData.PVA","page":"Home","text":"Position, Velocity, Attitude message. Corresponds to ASPN convention in aspn_schema/measurement_position_velocity_attitude.schema.json.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.PVA"},{"category":"type","location":"#RadarData.PNT","page":"Home","text":"Position, navigation, and timing data. Float64 was chosen to reduce precision errors in position and timing.\n\necef = Earth-Centered, Earth-Fixed coordinate. velenums = Velocity of platform in local East-North-Up coordinates. attitude = rotation of body frame relative to local NED coordinate frame. time_s = Time of measurement, in seconds. Typically maintained relative to reference time.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.PNT"},{"category":"type","location":"#RadarData.PNTHistory","page":"Home","text":"PNT history maintains a buffer of previous `max_states` PNT states.\n\ncurrent_end is an index indicating the last-stored state. When current_end exceeds max_states, current_end is reset to 1 and the buffer begins overwriting the oldest elements. Also includes ref_time_s; all contained states are assumed to have time_s relative to this time.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.PNTHistory"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.receive_pva!","page":"Home","text":"receive_pva!(history, pva)\n\nReceive a position, velocity, acceleration message. Overwrites the oldest state if PNTHistory has reached its maximum size.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.receive_pva!"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.interp_states","page":"Home","text":"interp_states(history, time_s)\n\nReturn best linearly interpolated estimate of state at the relative input time, in seconds. Assumes time_s is a single float or is sorted in increasing order. No extrapolation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.interp_states"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.interp_ecef","page":"Home","text":"interp_ecef(history, time_s)\n\nInterpolate ECEF field of position history for multiple times.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.interp_ecef"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.range_to_point","page":"Home","text":"range_to_point(pnt,ecef)\n\nCompute one-way range (m) from PNT to ECEF coordinate.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.range_to_point"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.range_rate_to_point","page":"Home","text":"range_rate_to_point(pnt, ecef)\n\nCompute one-way range (m) and one-way change in range (m/s) from PNT to ECEF coordinate.\n\n\n\n\n\nrange_rate_to_point(pnt, enu, ecef_ref)\n\nCompute one-way range (m) and one-way change in range (m/s) from PNT to ENU coordinate.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.range_rate_to_point"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.cart_to_horizon","page":"Home","text":"cart_to_horizon(cart_pos)\n\nConvert Cartesian coordinates stored as a 3 x N array to horizontal coordinates, (range, azimuth, elevation). Azimuth is measured as the angle with the x-axis, elevation is measured from the xy-plane. Angles are in radians.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.cart_to_horizon"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.cart_to_horizon_unwrap","page":"Home","text":"cart_to_horizon_unwrap(cart_pos)\n\nConvert Cartesian coordinates stored as a 3 x N array to horizontal coordinates, (range, azimuth, elevation). Azimuth is measured as the angle with the x-axis, elevation is measured from the xy-plane. Angles are in radians. Azimuth and elevation angles are unwrapped using DSP.unwrap.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.cart_to_horizon_unwrap"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.horizon_to_cart","page":"Home","text":"horizon_to_cart(horz_pos)\n\nConvert horizontal coordinates stored as a 3 x N array to Cartesian coordinates. Angles are assumed to be in radians.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.horizon_to_cart"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.azimuth_rad","page":"Home","text":"azimuth_rad(bisectors)\n\nThe unwrapped azimuth angle associated with the bistatic bisector stored in each column of input, in radians.\n\n\n\n\n\nCompute azimuth look direction, in radians.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.azimuth_rad"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.elevation_rad","page":"Home","text":"elevation_rad(bisectors)\n\nThe unwrapped elevation angle associated with the bistatic bisector stored in each column of input, in radians.\n\n\n\n\n\nCompute elevation look direction, in radians.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.elevation_rad"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.slant_plane_rot_2D","page":"Home","text":"slant_plane_rot_2D(bisectors)\n\nCompute rotation matrix to align bisectors to form a slant-plane-aligned ground-plane image. This centers the bisectors in azimuth.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.slant_plane_rot_2D"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.slant_plane_rot_3D","page":"Home","text":"slant_plane_rot_3D(bisectors, align_roll = false)\n\nCompute rotation matrix to align bisectors to form a slant-plane aligned image. By default, the rotation will only rotate in the azimuth and elevation directions. To also correct for a residual roll angle between the ground plane and the slant plane, set align_roll = true.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.slant_plane_rot_3D"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.ned_to_enu","page":"Home","text":"ned_to_enu(ned)\n\nConvert North-East-Down coordinates to East-North-Up.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.ned_to_enu"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.body_to_ecef","page":"Home","text":"body_to_ecef(ned)\n\nConvert body coordinates to ECEF orientations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.body_to_ecef"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.enu_rotation","page":"Home","text":"enu_rotation(lla)\n\nCompute rotation matrix from local ENU coordinates to ECEF coordinates, given lla as origin of ENU frame. ecef = R * enu + ecef_ref ENU coordinate axes are described by the columns of R.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.enu_rotation"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.intersect_los_plane","page":"Home","text":"intersect_los_plane(body_los, pnt, ground_hae_m = 0)\n\nCompute intersection of line of sight vector relative to body frame with ENU plane referenced to pnt.ecef, and return ENU coordinate. Ground plane is assumed to have given height above ellipsoid (HAE).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.intersect_los_plane"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.synth_chirp","page":"Home","text":"synth_chirp(sample_rate_hz, bandwidth_hz, duration_ns, carrier_hz = 0, start_phase_normalized = 0)\n\nSynthesize chirp given sample rate in Hz, bandwidth in Hz, and duration of the waveform in nanoseconds. start_phase_normalized is a phase offset in cycles, in the range [0,1). Input a negative bandwidth_hz to return a down-chirp.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.synth_chirp"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.synth_chirp!","page":"Home","text":"synth_chirp!(chirp, sample_rate_hz, bandwidth_hz, duration_ns, carrier_hz = 0, start_phase_normalized = 0)\n\nSynthesize chirp given sample rate in Hz, bandwidth in Hz, and duration of the waveform in nanoseconds. start_phase_normalized is a phase offset in cycles, in the range [0,1). Input a negative bandwidth_hz to return a down-chirp.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.synth_chirp!"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.range_compress","page":"Home","text":"range_compress(iq_data, ref_waveform_fft; downsample_rate = 1)\n\nApply FFT-based convolution to columns of iq_data with FFT of a reference waveform.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.range_compress"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.range_compress!","page":"Home","text":"range_compress!(iq_data, ref_waveform_fft)\n\nApply FFT-based convolution to columns of iq_data with FFT of a reference waveform. This version operates in-place, and so does not offer down-sampling or appropriate padding and trucation.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.range_compress!"},{"category":"type","location":"#RadarData.ImagePlane","page":"Home","text":"ImagePlane\n\nEnum specifying the image focus plane convention.\n\nValues:\n\nGROUND_PLANE: Image plane coincides with ENU ground plane (z=0)\nFIXED_EL_PLANE: Slant plane for constant-elevation flight through aperture center\nSLANT_PLANE: Best-fit plane to VPH bisector vectors\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.ImagePlane"},{"category":"type","location":"#RadarData.PFAKnots","page":"Home","text":"Polar Format Algorithm Knots data structure.\n\nThis structure holds metadata relevant to the formation and inversion of polar format images.\n\nspatial_freqs::Vector{Float64}: Frequency list, radians/meter\nbisectors::Matrix{Float64}: Bistatic bisector vectors (3 x num_pulses)\nref_range_m::Vector{Float64}: Two-way reference range per pulse, in meters\nslow_time_s::Vector{Float64}: Time relative to reference time, per pulse, in seconds\nref_time_s::Float64: Reference time, in seconds since Unix Epoch\nk_center::StaticArraysCore.SVector{2, Float64}: Spatial frequency center, removed for basebanding (radians/meter)\nexp_inds::StaticArraysCore.SVector{2, Float64}: Frequency and slow-time indices which correspond to k-center\nkx_image::Vector{Float64}: Spatial frequency in first dimension, uniformly spaced for imaging (radians/meter)\nky_image::Vector{Float64}: Spatial frequency in second dimension, uniformly spaced for imaging (radians/meter)\nx_image::Vector{Float64}: Image axis first dimension, meters. Range for slant plane aligned imagery.\ny_image::Vector{Float64}: Image axis second dimension, meters. Cross range for slant plane aligned imagery.\nslant_plane_rot::StaticArraysCore.SMatrix{3, 3, Float64}: Rotation from ENU to slant plane\ntx_poly::StaticArraysCore.SMatrix{3, 3, Float64}: Polynomial coefficients for slant-plane-aligned transmitter position\nkernel_sign::Float64: FFT sign convention, default is -1\nseparable::Bool: Whether to use separable interpolation or joint interpolation\ninner_box::Bool: Whether to use an inner box in frequency domain or outer box\nquadratic::Bool: Whether to apply quadratic phase error correction\ndistortion::Bool: Whether to correct the characteristic PFA distortion by resampling the image\nimage_plane::ImagePlane: Choice of focus plane for image, see ImagePlane enum for options\nenu_align::Bool: Resamples to align image with VPH sensor coordinate convention (ENU)\ncomp_poly::StaticArraysCore.SVector{3, Float64}: Derived quantity, range, rate, etc. of the sensor at aperture center\nradius_start::Vector{Float64}: Derived quantity, starting index for radial interpolation\nradius_delta::Vector{Float64}: Derived quantity, index step for radial interpolation\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.PFAKnots"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.compute_vph_center","page":"Home","text":"compute_vph_center(k_center, spatial_freqs, bisectors) -> Vector{Float64}\n\nFind VPH [frequencyindex, pulseindex] corresponding to k-space center. Uses nonlinear optimization to match k_center with interpolated VPH bisector geometry.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.compute_vph_center"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.fft_spacing","page":"Home","text":"fft_spacing(fft_len)\n\nRelative indices for window of length fft_len centered on the DC-bin of an equivalently sized FFT.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.fft_spacing"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.sfft","page":"Home","text":"sfft(in_array, [dims])\n\nSymmetric FFT, equivalent to fftshift(fft(ifftshift(input)))\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.sfft"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.sifft","page":"Home","text":"sifft(in_array, [dims])\n\nSymmetric IFFT, equivalent to fftshift(ifft(ifftshift(input)))\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.sifft"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.vph_to_rd","page":"Home","text":"vph_to_rd(in_array, kernel_sign = -1)\n\nCreate a range-Doppler image from VPH.data using FFTs / IFFTs according to VPH.kernel_sign. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.vph_to_rd"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.rd_to_vph","page":"Home","text":"rd_to_vph(in_array, kernel_sign = -1)\n\nConvert complex range-Doppler image back to spatial frequency domain (VPH.data domain)  using FFTs / IFFTs based on VPH.kernel_sign. \n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.rd_to_vph"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.center_freq","page":"Home","text":"centerfreq(freqlist_hz)\n\n\n\n\n\ncenter_freq(vph)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.center_freq"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.spatial_freqs","page":"Home","text":"spatial_freqs(freqs)\n\nFor frequency freqs in Hz, return the spatial frequency 2πf/c.\n\n\n\n\n\nspatial_freqs(vph)\n\nFor frequency freqs in Hz, return the spatial frequency 2πf/c.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.spatial_freqs"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.bandwidth","page":"Home","text":"bandwidth(freq_list_hz)\n\nReturn the bandwidth represented by equispaced freq_list_hz.\n\n\n\n\n\nbandwidth(vph)\n\nReturn the bandwidth spanned by VPH.freq_list_hz.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.bandwidth"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.range_res","page":"Home","text":"range_res(bandwidth)\n\nGiven bandwidth in Hz, compute two-way range resolution in meters. Note that this value will not change for upsampled range profiles.\n\n\n\n\n\nrange_res(vph)\n\nCompute two-way range resolution in meters.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.range_res"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.velocity_res","page":"Home","text":"velocity_res(center_freq)\n\nGiven center_freq in Hz, compute two-way velocity resolution in meters per pulse.\n\n\n\n\n\nvelocity_res(vph)\n\nCompute two-way velocity resolution in meters per pulse.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.velocity_res"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.range_axis","page":"Home","text":"range_axis(range_step, num_bins)\n\nCompute range axis (meters) of range-Doppler image given the range step and number of range bins.\n\n\n\n\n\nrange_axis(vph)\n\nCompute range axis (two-way meters) of range-Doppler image formed from VPH.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.range_axis"},{"category":"function","location":"#RadarData.velocity_axis","page":"Home","text":"velocity_axis(vel_step, num_bins)\n\nCompute velocity axis (m/pulse) of range-Doppler image formed from VPH.\n\n\n\n\n\nvelocity_axis(vph)\n\nCompute velocity axis (m/pulse) of range-Doppler image formed from VPH.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"RadarData.velocity_axis"}]
}
